WEBVTT

00:42.042 --> 00:46.963
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:04.230 --> 01:05.106
No.

01:05.190 --> 01:06.024
Get him!

01:09.486 --> 01:10.320
No.

01:26.836 --> 01:29.172
No…

01:29.255 --> 01:30.757
Oh, no…

01:30.840 --> 01:32.091
What do I do?

02:07.127 --> 02:08.336
Hello?

02:10.130 --> 02:10.964
What?

02:11.047 --> 02:12.924
From the Barun Cultural Foundation…

02:13.007 --> 02:14.300
You didn't know either?

02:14.384 --> 02:15.552
No, I didn't.

02:15.635 --> 02:17.011
Where's it being held?

02:17.095 --> 02:18.263
I'm on my way now.

02:18.346 --> 02:21.057
No, don't come here.
There are a lot of reporters here.

02:21.141 --> 02:23.351
What's important is that he's not here.

02:27.564 --> 02:30.233
Former Presidential Spokesperson
Paik Sa-eon announced

02:30.316 --> 02:33.444
he'd donate all the assets he inherited
from the late Chairman Paik Jang-ho

02:33.528 --> 02:34.737
to society this morning.

02:35.363 --> 02:37.824
And that all legal procedures

02:37.907 --> 02:40.869
will only be carried out
through his legal representative.

02:41.494 --> 02:44.956
Meanwhile, the Presidential Office
has accepted Paik's resignation

02:45.039 --> 02:47.375
and is seeking a replacement.

03:07.353 --> 03:08.229
LETTER OF APPOINTMENT

03:08.313 --> 03:09.147
He…

03:10.523 --> 03:11.691
disappeared.

03:15.320 --> 03:17.155
FINAL EPISODE

03:24.037 --> 03:25.288
Let's eat!

03:27.165 --> 03:28.291
Hurry and take a seat.

03:28.958 --> 03:29.792
Be careful.

03:32.712 --> 03:33.546
That's nice.

03:34.297 --> 03:35.381
Eat up.

03:35.465 --> 03:36.925
Is it okay to eat more?

03:37.008 --> 03:37.967
Of course.

03:38.551 --> 03:39.719
You have to eat to grow.

03:39.802 --> 03:42.263
I'm going to be taller than Sang-woo!

03:42.347 --> 03:43.806
I'll be cooler too.

03:43.890 --> 03:46.935
So, you can't marry Sang-woo, okay?

03:47.018 --> 03:48.102
- "Marry"?
- Here.

03:49.562 --> 03:50.772
Don't grow up so fast.

03:50.855 --> 03:52.607
Being cute is the best.

04:12.377 --> 04:13.836
Why compete with a kid?

04:15.546 --> 04:16.381
Compete…

04:17.340 --> 04:18.174
Whatever.

04:22.887 --> 04:24.055
Have you heard?

04:25.473 --> 04:27.433
Paik Sa-eon donated all his assets.

04:28.434 --> 04:29.269
I heard.

04:30.103 --> 04:31.896
How could I not know? It was huge.

04:33.022 --> 04:34.649
The director here said

04:35.483 --> 04:37.860
the Nuri Dream Center
is also getting a donation.

04:37.944 --> 04:38.903
From Sa-eon?

04:38.987 --> 04:40.989
It's from an anonymous donor.

04:41.823 --> 04:42.949
Who else could it be?

04:46.327 --> 04:48.121
He donated his assets,

04:48.621 --> 04:50.081
resigned as spokesperson,

04:50.665 --> 04:51.499
and is unreachable.

04:51.582 --> 04:53.042
No one knows where he is.

04:53.626 --> 04:55.545
It feels like Paik Sa-eon

04:56.963 --> 04:59.632
has completely disappeared from the world.

04:59.716 --> 05:00.633
He has.

05:03.636 --> 05:04.971
Paik Sa-eon's dead.

05:09.767 --> 05:10.935
That's right.

05:11.019 --> 05:12.520
He died.

05:19.652 --> 05:20.570
Breaking news.

05:20.653 --> 05:24.073
It has been confirmed that Hong Hee-joo,
the wife of Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon…

05:24.157 --> 05:24.991
1 MONTH AGO

05:25.074 --> 05:26.617
…has safely returned to her family

05:26.701 --> 05:29.120
after being missing for four days.

05:30.830 --> 05:32.373
Police have charged Shim Kyu-jin,

05:32.457 --> 05:35.376
the wife of Liberty and Justice Party
candidate Paik Ui-yong,

05:35.460 --> 05:39.422
with kidnapping and inciting murder
in connection with Hong Hee-joo's case.

05:39.505 --> 05:41.007
Min was also taken into custody

05:41.090 --> 05:43.593
and is being investigated
for carrying out the crime.

05:43.676 --> 05:47.388
Min confessed that he was instructed
to push the vehicle into the river

05:47.472 --> 05:48.765
to stage a fall

05:48.848 --> 05:53.019
and to scatter Hong Hee-joo's belongings,
such as her shoes and cell phone,

05:53.102 --> 05:55.438
to obstruct the police investigation.

05:55.521 --> 05:57.857
Meanwhile, the suspect
who kidnapped Hong Hee-joo

05:57.940 --> 06:02.320
repeatedly threatened the victim
with a firearm despite repeated warnings

06:02.403 --> 06:06.157
and ultimately was shot to death
by the police at the scene.

06:20.088 --> 06:22.006
Mom!

06:27.053 --> 06:29.680
Mom!

06:38.606 --> 06:39.899
You're there, aren't you?

06:42.193 --> 06:43.778
I know you're out there!

06:44.529 --> 06:48.866
Why did you lock me in here?

06:56.916 --> 06:59.168
How long will you keep me locked up?

06:59.752 --> 07:01.170
I told you.

07:01.963 --> 07:03.047
Son, I…

07:04.465 --> 07:06.551
I never want to lose you again.

07:10.179 --> 07:11.556
I regretted it so much.

07:12.723 --> 07:14.016
If only

07:14.892 --> 07:16.394
I had protected you back then,

07:17.478 --> 07:19.689
I wouldn't have lost you like that.

07:25.445 --> 07:26.612
Sa-eon,

07:27.405 --> 07:28.865
listen to me carefully.

07:29.991 --> 07:30.825
Listen.

07:32.285 --> 07:33.786
I'm not locking you up,

07:36.080 --> 07:37.498
I'm protecting you.

08:09.197 --> 08:11.199
KIDNAPPING SUSPECT SHOT TO DEATH

09:11.842 --> 09:12.718
All this time,

09:14.720 --> 09:17.974
I've always believed
that I lived a luckier life than others.

09:18.683 --> 09:20.476
With a prestigious political family

09:21.644 --> 09:23.980
and a father respected…

09:25.982 --> 09:27.149
by the entire nation.

09:37.368 --> 09:38.953
But it was all a lie.

09:40.204 --> 09:41.455
The truth about my father

09:42.373 --> 09:44.959
was the complete opposite
of what I had believed.

09:45.042 --> 09:46.252
It was an illusion.

09:46.335 --> 09:50.214
The son I had thought to be dead returned

09:50.965 --> 09:52.675
and made it more miserable.

09:53.259 --> 09:58.472
So, I am leaving behind
my family and background,

09:59.473 --> 10:03.060
and I will stand again as Paik Ui-yong,
an ordinary man.

10:04.312 --> 10:05.938
Honorable citizens,

10:07.773 --> 10:09.775
if you can generously embrace…

10:11.652 --> 10:13.696
my shortcomings and mistakes,

10:13.779 --> 10:15.156
I, Paik Ui-yong,

10:15.865 --> 10:19.076
promise to be reborn…

10:20.870 --> 10:23.289
as a better version of myself for you.

11:54.839 --> 11:57.925
Paik Ui-yong came in third
with 3.4% of the vote.

11:58.008 --> 11:59.468
In the end,

11:59.552 --> 12:02.096
the Paik family
never produced a president.

12:02.680 --> 12:05.766
The defendant murdered her father-in-law

12:05.850 --> 12:09.687
and, showing no signs of remorse,
once again incited murder,

12:10.438 --> 12:14.400
ultimately repeating a crime
that led to casualties.

12:14.483 --> 12:15.484
JUDGE

12:15.568 --> 12:18.612
This court holds the defendant
accountable for this,

12:18.696 --> 12:20.948
and sentences Shim Kyu-jin

12:21.657 --> 12:23.409
to life in prison.

12:32.084 --> 12:35.045
In the end, the mother,
who failed twice to protect her son,

12:35.671 --> 12:36.839
appealed.

12:39.508 --> 12:43.220
She asked for the maximum sentence,
the death penalty.

12:51.145 --> 12:54.190
The butler, who had been loyal
to the Paik family his whole life,

12:54.273 --> 12:56.942
acknowledged his crime
and showed deep remorse.

12:57.026 --> 13:00.070
Considering that the victim
did not wish to punish him,

13:00.696 --> 13:03.073
he was sentenced to five years in prison.

13:08.537 --> 13:12.041
The Paik family's scandal,
which had caused such an uproar,

13:13.000 --> 13:14.835
came to an end.

13:34.355 --> 13:35.481
As for him,

13:36.148 --> 13:38.150
he disappeared from the world,

13:39.360 --> 13:41.820
letting go of everything he had.

13:54.375 --> 13:55.376
You're back.

13:55.459 --> 13:58.212
Have you been well?

14:02.841 --> 14:04.510
Why do you keep coming here?

14:05.970 --> 14:07.221
You know very well…

14:08.889 --> 14:10.849
that I betrayed the spokesperson.

14:12.017 --> 14:13.644
Before he realized your betrayal,

14:15.646 --> 14:17.815
he called you the most

14:19.525 --> 14:21.944
and talked to you the most.

14:24.405 --> 14:26.115
Yes, he did.

14:26.699 --> 14:27.783
Anything is fine.

14:28.742 --> 14:32.288
Does anything from your conversations
with him come to mind? Anything.

14:34.790 --> 14:35.875
Please, tell me.

14:39.044 --> 14:40.212
He said…

14:41.255 --> 14:43.257
he'd disappear like dust.

14:44.258 --> 14:45.801
Once the revenge was over

14:46.719 --> 14:48.971
and with everything
that had driven his life,

14:50.431 --> 14:52.808
his goals and targets, gone,

14:54.727 --> 14:56.478
he said he would self-destruct.

14:58.355 --> 14:59.273
Originally.

15:02.902 --> 15:03.944
"Originally"?

15:05.362 --> 15:06.572
Yes, but…

15:07.323 --> 15:08.407
What about now?

15:09.325 --> 15:10.910
Did you change your mind?

15:12.119 --> 15:12.953
Of course.

15:15.080 --> 15:17.124
I'm going to live a life
after taking revenge.

15:18.292 --> 15:19.293
With the person

15:21.003 --> 15:23.213
I want to be with for the rest of my life.

15:24.256 --> 15:30.429
So I don't think he disappeared
just because the revenge was over.

15:32.014 --> 15:32.932
I'm sure…

15:34.516 --> 15:36.435
there's another reason.

15:48.864 --> 15:50.699
- Hee-joo.
- Mr. Kang.

15:51.283 --> 15:53.535
How long has it been?

15:53.619 --> 15:54.703
Have you been well…

16:00.376 --> 16:01.710
It's been a while.

16:03.545 --> 16:05.589
Are you here to see Mr. Park?

16:06.298 --> 16:08.050
Yeah, I come by often.

16:09.009 --> 16:11.762
It frustrates me
when I think of the spokesperson,

16:12.596 --> 16:15.724
but I was taught to hate sin
and not people.

16:19.061 --> 16:19.979
See you later.

16:22.189 --> 16:23.691
He used to ask me quite often.

16:25.442 --> 16:30.364
He asked what married couples talk about
and how they show affection.

16:32.282 --> 16:35.869
And how to be a good husband.

16:35.953 --> 16:37.287
In your marriage,

16:37.913 --> 16:40.082
do you hide anything

16:40.749 --> 16:42.376
or deceive each other?

16:42.960 --> 16:46.588
Sometimes it's necessary to pretend
not to know and let things slide.

16:47.172 --> 16:49.758
Marriage takes effort, don't you think?

16:50.551 --> 16:51.719
Effort?

16:51.802 --> 16:54.430
How do you do that?

16:54.513 --> 16:56.432
- Excuse me?
- "I love you,

16:56.515 --> 16:58.434
ultimate love in the universe."

16:59.810 --> 17:01.145
He may have been clumsy,

17:02.813 --> 17:04.356
but he tried really hard.

17:11.822 --> 17:13.157
I want to hear more.

17:25.794 --> 17:26.754
The spokesperson…

17:28.630 --> 17:30.007
learned how to do this.

17:30.799 --> 17:32.217
Can you believe it?

17:32.968 --> 17:34.428
We were going to the retreat.

17:34.928 --> 17:38.724
On the bus,
he asked me how to show affection.

17:39.600 --> 17:41.101
So I taught him this.

17:41.935 --> 17:42.936
But I guess…

17:43.937 --> 17:45.439
that was all for you.

17:46.356 --> 17:48.525
I never imagined that.

17:49.109 --> 17:50.194
I miss him too.

18:00.913 --> 18:02.790
How handsome. It looks great on you.

18:04.792 --> 18:06.794
Dad, do you remember?

18:06.877 --> 18:10.923
When I was little,
you bought me tonkatsu every Christmas.

18:11.006 --> 18:13.008
Tonkatsu is yummy.

18:14.802 --> 18:19.723
I ate all sorts of delicious food
every Christmas at Chairman Hong's house,

18:20.349 --> 18:23.102
but the tonkatsu we shared together
was the best.

18:23.185 --> 18:25.813
I like tonkatsu.
That's why I asked to come here.

18:27.231 --> 18:28.649
It was my idea to come here.

18:28.732 --> 18:30.484
Your food's ready.

18:30.567 --> 18:31.902
Thank you.

18:36.698 --> 18:37.991
You're back again.

18:38.700 --> 18:39.701
Enjoy your meal.

18:50.712 --> 18:51.547
It's good.

18:51.630 --> 18:53.465
- But, Dad?
- Yeah.

18:53.549 --> 18:54.883
Have you been here before?

18:55.384 --> 18:56.510
On my birthday.

18:56.593 --> 18:57.886
I asked to come here.

18:59.096 --> 19:00.180
Asked who?

19:01.265 --> 19:02.182
My son-in-law.

19:07.479 --> 19:08.438
What?

20:03.702 --> 20:07.247
When was that?
If it was your birthday, was it July?

20:10.042 --> 20:13.295
Has he come back since? Have you seen him?

20:55.420 --> 20:56.255
Let's go.

21:06.974 --> 21:08.558
It's almost Christmas.

21:10.060 --> 21:12.229
Don't stay alone in an empty house.

21:12.896 --> 21:14.147
Come with me.

21:16.775 --> 21:19.695
If you don't want to see Mom and Dad,
let's go on a trip.

21:20.946 --> 21:22.990
How long are you going to stay here?

21:24.658 --> 21:26.535
How many times do I have to tell you?

21:27.327 --> 21:28.870
I'm not leaving this house.

21:28.954 --> 21:30.414
You'll keep waiting here?

21:31.373 --> 21:33.292
It's been six months already.

21:35.335 --> 21:36.878
What if I leave this house,

21:37.963 --> 21:39.172
and he comes back?

21:40.841 --> 21:41.675
What if he comes,

21:43.093 --> 21:45.679
but I'm not here, and we miss each other?

21:47.431 --> 21:48.849
In-a…

21:51.143 --> 21:54.313
I still can't believe he's gone.

21:55.355 --> 21:58.900
After I was rescued
and woke up in the hospital, I'm sure…

22:01.320 --> 22:02.738
he was right next to me.

22:09.703 --> 22:13.623
When I slept for days from exhaustion,

22:19.296 --> 22:20.380
every time I woke up,

22:21.173 --> 22:23.050
he was right next to me,

22:25.260 --> 22:26.803
as if he'd always be there.

22:42.736 --> 22:43.570
And…

22:44.780 --> 22:47.574
on the last night I could remember…

22:47.657 --> 22:48.575
Hee-joo.

22:49.159 --> 22:50.494
Hee-joo.

22:57.542 --> 22:58.835
It's okay.

22:58.919 --> 23:01.004
It was just a dream, okay?

23:03.090 --> 23:04.299
I'm so relieved.

23:07.803 --> 23:10.847
I had a dream that you got shot.

23:13.517 --> 23:14.476
No.

23:15.143 --> 23:16.603
I'm right here.

23:18.230 --> 23:19.314
So go back to sleep.

23:42.295 --> 23:46.216
I still remember his warm touch
that lulled me to sleep so vividly.

23:47.175 --> 23:50.428
I feel like he'll come right back.
How could I leave this house?

23:50.512 --> 23:51.763
He's not coming back.

23:52.347 --> 23:53.223
What?

23:53.306 --> 23:55.934
I thought you'd give up and move on
after some time.

23:56.768 --> 23:57.602
But how is it…

23:58.854 --> 24:01.022
that you can't forget, not for a moment?

24:04.192 --> 24:05.443
Do you know?

24:06.069 --> 24:08.989
Do you know why he left
and isn't coming back?

24:09.072 --> 24:10.615
Do you know the reason?

24:12.200 --> 24:14.452
This is the only thing I can tell you.

24:16.246 --> 24:17.205
Forget him.

24:18.123 --> 24:18.957
He…

24:20.792 --> 24:21.960
will never come back.

24:22.586 --> 24:24.171
So why?

24:25.589 --> 24:27.799
Why would you say that?

24:28.508 --> 24:29.676
In-a, tell me.

24:30.343 --> 24:31.261
Please.

24:34.848 --> 24:35.682
Hee-joo.

24:38.101 --> 24:40.145
No matter what I say,
I know you won't listen.

24:41.146 --> 24:46.193
But now, I just want you
to hurt less and be happier.

24:47.194 --> 24:48.111
No.

24:57.829 --> 25:00.749
I can only hurt less and be happier

25:01.416 --> 25:03.084
if he's here.

25:07.047 --> 25:09.382
I need him so badly.

25:10.967 --> 25:13.470
I miss him so much.

25:54.886 --> 25:55.720
PAIK SA-EON

25:55.804 --> 25:57.305
Can we meet up for a moment?

25:59.474 --> 26:03.186
MEMORIAL OF PEACE AND HOPE

26:03.270 --> 26:06.606
WHERE YOUR LOVED ONES
WILL BE REMEMBERED FOREVER

26:07.232 --> 26:08.733
Why here?

26:33.717 --> 26:36.678
The number you called is not in service.

26:36.761 --> 26:39.222
Please check the number and try again.

26:45.687 --> 26:48.648
The number you called is not in service.

26:48.732 --> 26:51.192
Please check the number and try again.

26:53.153 --> 26:55.864
PAIK SA-EON

27:13.757 --> 27:15.967
INCOMING CALL
INTERNATIONAL CALL

27:17.552 --> 27:18.470
Hello?

27:24.017 --> 27:25.143
Hello?

27:37.947 --> 27:39.824
CALLS

27:46.748 --> 27:48.958
SEARCH HERE

27:49.042 --> 27:50.460
COUNTRY CODE 604

27:52.962 --> 27:56.841
ARGAN

27:57.967 --> 27:59.052
Argan?

28:08.812 --> 28:09.646
What?

28:10.313 --> 28:11.356
You got a call from Argan?

28:11.439 --> 28:13.191
Not just a call.

28:21.241 --> 28:22.158
Ms. Hong Hee-joo?

28:22.742 --> 28:23.660
Yes, that's me.

28:23.743 --> 28:24.577
Here you go.

28:25.286 --> 28:26.621
It's international mail.

28:26.704 --> 28:27.997
Can you sign this for me?

28:29.624 --> 28:30.625
Thank you.

29:03.116 --> 29:04.117
In my name?

29:23.261 --> 29:25.680
"Buiben International School
of Sign Language."

29:47.494 --> 29:49.204
How much did you donate?

29:49.287 --> 29:50.538
Two billion won.

29:51.831 --> 29:53.583
Two billion won?

29:56.002 --> 29:58.630
Wait, were you that loaded?

29:59.339 --> 30:01.257
It wasn't me.

30:01.341 --> 30:02.926
I don't have that kind of money.

30:03.551 --> 30:04.469
Then who…

30:04.552 --> 30:08.223
Didn't you work as a war correspondent
in Argan with him?

30:08.932 --> 30:11.601
Do you know of any places
he might be in Argan?

30:11.684 --> 30:13.394
What are you talking about?

30:14.521 --> 30:15.605
Paik Sa-eon!

30:19.025 --> 30:20.819
Are you saying he did this?

30:20.902 --> 30:22.195
Who else would do this?

30:22.904 --> 30:24.489
The call from Argan,

30:24.572 --> 30:27.575
the amount of two billion won,
406, and 604…

30:28.284 --> 30:29.619
Is this just a coincidence?

30:35.583 --> 30:37.168
I don't know what you're saying.

30:37.252 --> 30:39.921
So, what if I know some places in Argan?
Will you go--

30:40.004 --> 30:41.756
If you have any ideas, tell me.

30:42.715 --> 30:43.967
Come on, Hee-joo.

30:45.218 --> 30:46.886
Don't you know Argan's a war zone?

30:47.470 --> 30:49.514
Not only is it restricted
to certain people,

30:50.014 --> 30:51.724
but you'll die if you go!

30:51.808 --> 30:54.352
It doesn't matter if I die here
waiting for him

30:54.435 --> 30:55.979
or get shot over there.

30:56.062 --> 30:57.605
It's all the same to me.

30:58.857 --> 31:00.441
So, please tell me.

31:01.651 --> 31:03.319
I'm not leaving before you tell me.

31:18.626 --> 31:19.460
Sunset.

31:20.837 --> 31:21.880
Sunset?

31:21.963 --> 31:23.715
Haven't you seen his phone's lock screen?

31:24.465 --> 31:26.467
He's crazy about them.

31:27.677 --> 31:29.053
He's obsessed with sunsets.

31:30.847 --> 31:31.931
When we were in Argan,

31:32.557 --> 31:34.559
he'd rush over at sundown.

31:35.810 --> 31:37.896
There's an incredible spot
to watch the sunset.

31:39.063 --> 31:43.568
He'd take photo after photo
of the sunset sky there.

31:53.036 --> 31:56.748
It's red, like your swollen cheek.

32:10.136 --> 32:13.222
BUIBEN INTERNATIONAL SCHOOL
OF SIGN LANGUAGE, ARGAN

37:54.397 --> 37:57.900
I told you to wait
until I come to find you.

37:58.484 --> 37:59.902
So, why?

38:06.242 --> 38:07.493
Why are you here?

38:31.767 --> 38:32.893
Because of you…

38:35.980 --> 38:38.399
do you know how many times
my plans have changed?

38:41.277 --> 38:42.403
No, from the start,

38:43.696 --> 38:45.865
if you were involved,
none of my plans worked.

38:48.367 --> 38:49.869
It all just falls apart.

38:52.872 --> 38:54.040
Let it fall apart.

38:55.958 --> 38:57.293
I'll ruin everything.

39:00.504 --> 39:02.298
You're always going on about plans!

39:03.049 --> 39:03.883
So?

39:04.467 --> 39:06.761
Did anything in our relationship
go according to plan?

39:08.095 --> 39:09.680
It didn't for me.

39:10.264 --> 39:12.391
Divorcing you was my plan.

39:13.017 --> 39:14.226
You know what happened.

39:14.894 --> 39:16.187
I couldn't divorce you,

39:18.356 --> 39:20.274
I couldn't escape you,

39:21.192 --> 39:23.319
and now I can't live a single day
without you.

39:23.402 --> 39:26.280
So I traveled halfway around the world
to come here!

39:26.364 --> 39:27.531
Are you dumb?

39:28.115 --> 39:30.284
How could you say
you can't live without me?

39:30.368 --> 39:31.285
How…

39:32.036 --> 39:33.996
can you say that when you know everything?

39:36.248 --> 39:37.375
About what?

39:40.795 --> 39:43.506
This is the only thing I can tell you.

39:43.589 --> 39:44.673
He…

39:46.258 --> 39:47.468
will never come back.

39:48.344 --> 39:49.762
Did my sister say something?

39:51.806 --> 39:54.100
No. Before that…

40:09.990 --> 40:11.909
What did you find out that day?

40:14.120 --> 40:16.038
Why did you look at me like that?

40:16.747 --> 40:19.583
Answer me! What did he tell you?

40:22.545 --> 40:23.379
Did you know?

40:24.255 --> 40:26.090
Your father, Paik Jang-ho,

40:27.591 --> 40:29.260
killed Hong Hee-joo's little brother.

40:30.469 --> 40:31.303
Yeah.

40:31.929 --> 40:33.097
That car accident.

40:34.515 --> 40:35.933
Paik Jang-ho put out a hit

40:36.600 --> 40:38.686
and ran them over with a truck.

40:46.110 --> 40:48.696
Paik Jang-ho tried so hard
to hide me from the world,

40:49.822 --> 40:51.615
but her little brother saw me.

40:57.663 --> 40:59.915
From the blood running in my veins
to my name,

41:02.001 --> 41:03.711
the only thing I ever did right

41:05.546 --> 41:07.298
in this sinful life of mine

41:08.507 --> 41:10.384
was protect you, Hee-joo.

41:13.429 --> 41:16.599
THE LATE HONG YU-JIN

41:19.143 --> 41:20.352
But it turned out

41:21.145 --> 41:22.855
I didn't protect you.

41:23.522 --> 41:25.399
Instead, I took so much from you.

41:27.026 --> 41:28.110
Your brother,

41:29.028 --> 41:30.446
your youth,

41:31.197 --> 41:32.198
your dreams.

41:34.283 --> 41:37.161
My father was the one
who crushed them all.

41:49.548 --> 41:50.382
Did you…

41:52.176 --> 41:53.427
finally figure it out?

41:55.721 --> 41:56.680
What about Hee-joo?

41:59.850 --> 42:02.561
She knows everything.

42:04.813 --> 42:09.276
She knew everything,
yet she still risked her life for you.

42:34.552 --> 42:36.929
Is that why you left me?
Because you felt bad?

42:37.763 --> 42:39.014
I didn't leave you.

42:42.601 --> 42:44.520
I needed time to punish myself.

42:47.481 --> 42:49.066
I was looking for an excuse.

42:54.905 --> 42:56.407
Since you already knew everything

42:57.032 --> 42:58.701
and said it didn't matter,

43:00.327 --> 43:01.954
I kept rationalizing it.

43:02.705 --> 43:04.540
I thought I could just stay here,

43:06.917 --> 43:09.587
pretending not to know,

43:11.297 --> 43:12.881
and make you happy from now on.

43:16.468 --> 43:18.679
When did it even start
that I can't live without you?

43:19.805 --> 43:21.807
My goal was just…

43:22.975 --> 43:24.310
to set you free.

43:32.026 --> 43:33.027
And I felt…

43:35.362 --> 43:37.114
so disgusted with myself for it.

43:40.993 --> 43:42.411
So I wanted to punish myself,

43:43.787 --> 43:45.831
until I could forgive myself.

43:47.625 --> 43:49.835
How much longer do I have to wait?

43:52.129 --> 43:53.464
You know it too.

43:57.134 --> 43:59.845
We spent more time
misunderstanding and drifting apart

44:01.388 --> 44:04.141
than cherishing and loving each other.

44:05.351 --> 44:07.019
But if I still have to wait,

44:10.439 --> 44:12.358
how much longer will it take?

44:13.609 --> 44:17.696
If you have to be punished,
I should be the one to punish you!

44:20.991 --> 44:22.576
You're punishing me now.

44:24.620 --> 44:26.372
You're right in front of me,

44:29.041 --> 44:31.627
and I want to hold you like crazy.

44:33.545 --> 44:34.880
Can't you see I'm holding back?

44:40.094 --> 44:42.554
I won't hold back anymore.

47:29.221 --> 47:30.430
It was true.

47:37.521 --> 47:39.606
We lived together for three years,

47:40.357 --> 47:43.110
but I didn't know
because I never checked your phone.

47:45.529 --> 47:46.613
They're all sunsets.

47:47.990 --> 47:49.533
It was filled with you.

47:58.375 --> 48:00.210
Is that why you came to Argan?

48:03.755 --> 48:05.090
It was far from you,

48:08.051 --> 48:09.761
but it was where I could see you.

48:13.390 --> 48:14.725
But I never thought

48:16.351 --> 48:18.895
I'd see you here like this.

48:20.397 --> 48:21.732
604.

48:23.317 --> 48:25.402
You called me from that number, right?

48:29.114 --> 48:30.032
That day,

48:31.241 --> 48:32.451
I had a dream.

48:34.244 --> 48:36.788
You were crying a lot in the dream.

48:41.168 --> 48:42.085
So…

48:43.629 --> 48:45.964
Actually, that was just an excuse.

48:46.048 --> 48:48.383
I just wanted to hear your voice.

48:51.720 --> 48:52.804
That being said,

48:54.264 --> 48:57.017
I didn't expect you
to just show up like this.

49:00.228 --> 49:04.650
Why did you make a donation
to the sign language school in my name?

49:05.692 --> 49:07.027
I donated two billion won.

49:08.195 --> 49:09.696
Does that remind you of something?

49:12.741 --> 49:13.575
Two billion won.

49:14.409 --> 49:17.871
One, the groom cannot initiate a divorce.

49:17.954 --> 49:21.333
Two, divorce is prohibited
under any circumstances.

49:21.416 --> 49:24.169
Three, we will actively announce
to the public

49:24.252 --> 49:26.088
that we are a married couple.

49:26.171 --> 49:28.090
If any of these are violated,

49:28.840 --> 49:30.967
the penalty will be two billion won.

49:32.886 --> 49:33.804
That's right.

49:34.554 --> 49:36.014
It's my settlement to you.

49:40.519 --> 49:42.104
Because I'm going to break

49:43.897 --> 49:45.482
our wedding vows.

49:48.235 --> 49:49.820
Paik Sa-eon…

49:52.239 --> 49:54.074
will divorce Hong Hee-joo.

49:56.284 --> 49:57.119
What?

49:57.202 --> 49:59.579
And I, not Paik Sa-eon…

50:05.043 --> 50:06.420
will marry you.

51:10.108 --> 51:12.402
- Do you want to switch spots?
- What? Why?

51:13.069 --> 51:16.740
Well, the spokesperson
will come out when this door opens.

51:16.823 --> 51:20.994
I'm feeling a bit overwhelmed and nervous.

51:21.077 --> 51:22.996
- Will you switch spots with me?
- Nope.

51:23.079 --> 51:24.498
This isn't the Presidential Office.

51:24.581 --> 51:27.167
He's not the spokesperson anymore.
Don't be nervous.

51:28.126 --> 51:29.085
Right?

51:29.169 --> 51:30.295
Right…

51:33.048 --> 51:33.882
Hello.

51:33.965 --> 51:35.091
For you.

51:35.175 --> 51:36.009
Get in here.

51:37.469 --> 51:38.804
I'm starving.

51:38.887 --> 51:41.223
- Wow!
- Look at that.

51:43.725 --> 51:44.559
Goodness.

51:48.605 --> 51:49.731
The food keeps coming.

51:50.941 --> 51:52.400
Hee-joo, did you make all of this?

51:53.360 --> 51:56.029
- Amazing. Everything tastes delicious.
- Yes.

51:56.112 --> 51:57.864
- I made it.
- What?

51:58.657 --> 52:00.158
- You did?
- You?

52:00.242 --> 52:03.787
Are you saying you won't let your wife
lift a finger from now on?

52:03.870 --> 52:05.372
I've taught you well.

52:08.500 --> 52:09.918
It's not that.

52:10.001 --> 52:12.045
She's not very good at cook--

52:14.714 --> 52:15.799
Oh, my.

52:15.882 --> 52:17.884
Your ring is so pretty.

52:17.968 --> 52:19.386
Give me your hand.

52:20.345 --> 52:21.805
Look at that.

52:21.888 --> 52:24.349
Your ring is beautiful.

52:25.016 --> 52:27.269
But I just don't get it.

52:27.352 --> 52:30.272
Why get married twice,
especially to the same person?

52:30.939 --> 52:32.107
I know.

52:32.190 --> 52:33.108
However,

52:33.191 --> 52:34.734
I approve of this marriage.

52:35.777 --> 52:38.029
Congratulations! The fruit of true love.

52:38.113 --> 52:39.197
Thank you.

52:40.574 --> 52:42.409
By the way, is it true?

52:42.492 --> 52:44.327
- Did you change your name?
- You did?

52:45.036 --> 52:46.121
To what?

52:46.204 --> 52:47.581
Well…

52:50.166 --> 52:52.002
Paik Yu-yeon.

52:52.085 --> 52:54.004
Paik Yu-yeon?

52:55.505 --> 52:56.756
What does it mean?

52:58.466 --> 53:00.302
Yu is for "only."

53:00.385 --> 53:01.803
Yeon is for "love."

53:03.346 --> 53:08.018
A one and only love in the world?

53:08.852 --> 53:10.520
Oh, my.

53:11.438 --> 53:13.315
Hey. Are these your true colors?

53:18.486 --> 53:20.280
Why are you looking at me like that?

53:20.363 --> 53:23.658
Congratulations on becoming
the most romantic husband.

53:25.327 --> 53:28.872
So, tell us, when will you return
to the Presidential Office?

53:30.123 --> 53:31.499
I won't be returning there.

53:32.208 --> 53:33.877
Then what will you do?

53:39.299 --> 53:42.135
Anyway, even though
it's hard to get used to,

53:42.218 --> 53:44.638
let's celebrate Paik Yu-yeon

53:45.305 --> 53:47.557
and Hong Hee-joo's marriage.

53:47.641 --> 53:48.600
Shall we all toast?

53:48.683 --> 53:50.644
- Congratulations!
- Congrats.

53:50.727 --> 53:51.770
Thank you.

53:52.938 --> 53:53.939
While we're at it,

53:55.065 --> 53:56.399
will you congratulate us too?

53:56.483 --> 53:58.026
To tell you the truth…

53:59.027 --> 53:59.945
We're also…

54:01.321 --> 54:02.364
getting married!

54:03.573 --> 54:05.825
- Wow!
- Seriously?

54:06.993 --> 54:08.453
Na You-ri!

54:08.536 --> 54:10.705
Congratulations, You-ri!

54:10.789 --> 54:11.623
Sang-woo!

54:11.706 --> 54:12.874
Thank you.

54:12.958 --> 54:15.126
I had no idea.

54:15.627 --> 54:16.628
Congratulations.

54:17.212 --> 54:18.463
Congrats.

54:18.546 --> 54:19.673
Congratulations.

54:19.756 --> 54:21.424
You two look great together.

54:21.508 --> 54:22.842
Let's toast!

54:23.677 --> 54:25.595
- Congratulations!
- Yeah, congrats!

54:27.389 --> 54:28.807
Being married is nice, right?

54:28.890 --> 54:29.724
What?

54:30.558 --> 54:32.560
Of course, it is.

54:32.644 --> 54:33.520
Right?

54:33.603 --> 54:35.230
Of course. You-ri, it's good.

54:39.192 --> 54:40.068
What are you doing?

54:42.153 --> 54:42.988
Hey!

55:21.401 --> 55:22.318
Are you tired?

55:24.821 --> 55:27.323
You said you did all the cooking.

55:27.949 --> 55:29.409
But it's true.

55:35.957 --> 55:37.042
Great job.

55:37.125 --> 55:39.085
The lively atmosphere was nice.

55:40.420 --> 55:44.841
I hope this house stays lively
and never quiet.

55:45.675 --> 55:46.509
Really?

55:47.135 --> 55:50.430
Then, we need someone other than us here.

55:52.057 --> 55:54.434
I start work at the broadcast station
next week.

55:54.517 --> 55:56.019
- The station?
- Yeah.

55:56.102 --> 55:59.022
I've agreed to be
their sign language interpreter again.

55:59.647 --> 56:01.649
And I'm going to continue doing it.

56:02.233 --> 56:03.359
I like this job.

56:04.194 --> 56:05.904
Sure. Congrats.

56:11.201 --> 56:12.577
Cooperate, Hong Hee-joo.

56:13.286 --> 56:15.121
If you want this house to be lively,

56:15.663 --> 56:17.165
we need more family members!

56:18.124 --> 56:19.292
What are you doing?

56:19.375 --> 56:20.877
Cooperate!

56:26.382 --> 56:27.801
JUAN RAW SEAFOOD

56:55.453 --> 56:56.538
Try it.

56:57.122 --> 56:59.165
It's your favorite.

57:00.792 --> 57:02.127
Since that day,

57:03.878 --> 57:05.630
I just can't eat fish anymore.

57:06.548 --> 57:07.924
When I smell the fishy odor,

57:09.509 --> 57:11.511
it brings back memories
of the fishing spot.

57:13.596 --> 57:14.848
Help…

57:19.644 --> 57:20.478
Help…

57:25.608 --> 57:27.152
I'll make you something else.

57:27.235 --> 57:28.069
No.

57:28.653 --> 57:29.487
It's fine.

57:45.670 --> 57:47.630
You're as good as ever.

57:49.048 --> 57:50.091
Thanks.

57:58.224 --> 57:59.559
Try the white kimchi.

58:01.436 --> 58:02.479
Marriage registration?

58:03.229 --> 58:05.273
I'll come back with him soon.

58:06.024 --> 58:07.108
He wanted to come today,

58:07.817 --> 58:10.403
but I didn't think
you'd say anything nice to him.

58:11.237 --> 58:12.363
You're right.

58:13.072 --> 58:16.284
You said you'd choose your own fate
and even went into that war zone.

58:16.367 --> 58:18.161
And you married him without telling us.

58:18.244 --> 58:19.078
Unbelievable.

58:20.246 --> 58:21.748
You said you never saw her smile.

58:24.000 --> 58:24.834
She's smiling now.

58:25.877 --> 58:26.878
She looks happy.

58:29.130 --> 58:30.632
What else could we ask for?

58:33.593 --> 58:35.762
Where do you live?

58:35.845 --> 58:37.639
The neighborhood's far from here.

58:38.806 --> 58:40.225
Where is it?

58:41.893 --> 58:43.394
Let's take it slow, Mom.

58:43.478 --> 58:45.104
I'll visit from time to time.

58:57.534 --> 58:58.535
Be happy.

59:01.204 --> 59:03.581
I know how much he cares for you.

59:05.208 --> 59:06.209
So live a long…

59:07.335 --> 59:08.628
and happy life.

59:24.060 --> 59:24.978
Hee-joo.

59:30.149 --> 59:32.485
I'm sorry I didn't tell you
about the marriage.

59:32.569 --> 59:33.403
But…

59:35.905 --> 59:37.865
I didn't know how you'd feel.

59:37.949 --> 59:39.492
I'm not trying to congratulate you.

59:40.493 --> 59:42.245
Since we reunited,

59:43.871 --> 59:47.125
I've been trying my best
to get closer to you.

59:48.042 --> 59:49.043
But…

59:50.628 --> 59:51.629
it was so hard.

59:54.299 --> 59:55.633
But when I think about it,

59:56.426 --> 59:58.177
I don't think I did it right.

59:59.095 --> 01:00:00.680
Before we could get close,

01:00:02.056 --> 01:00:03.850
I should've said this to you first.

01:00:07.437 --> 01:00:08.271
Hee-joo,

01:00:09.397 --> 01:00:10.231
I'm sorry.

01:00:11.316 --> 01:00:12.150
I…

01:00:14.569 --> 01:00:16.404
made you suffer for a long time,

01:00:17.447 --> 01:00:18.656
both as the perpetrator

01:00:19.907 --> 01:00:21.159
and the bystander.

01:00:25.121 --> 01:00:25.955
In-a.

01:00:27.665 --> 01:00:29.626
I'm going to forget everything
from the past.

01:00:30.460 --> 01:00:32.795
If I keep dwelling on the past,

01:00:34.255 --> 01:00:37.425
I'll be unhappy in the present.

01:00:38.676 --> 01:00:39.844
You should try it too.

01:00:40.595 --> 01:00:42.055
Forget the past.

01:00:43.640 --> 01:00:44.807
Would that be okay?

01:00:49.854 --> 01:00:50.855
In-a.

01:00:52.106 --> 01:00:53.650
I'm happy.

01:00:54.484 --> 01:00:55.526
And now,

01:00:56.110 --> 01:00:58.363
I don't doubt my happiness anymore.

01:01:00.990 --> 01:01:03.993
Because I'm someone who truly deserves it,

01:01:05.119 --> 01:01:06.996
and he helped me believe that.

01:01:08.456 --> 01:01:10.500
You deserve to be happy too.

01:01:11.876 --> 01:01:13.044
Believe me.

01:01:18.466 --> 01:01:19.467
Breaking news.

01:01:19.550 --> 01:01:22.428
The ongoing Paltima airstrikes
are taking place in Izmael,

01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:25.598
where Korean nationals have been kidnapped
by armed militants.

01:01:26.224 --> 01:01:30.603
In response, the government has set up
a Protection Headquarters

01:01:30.687 --> 01:01:34.399
at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs
and will send negotiator Paik Yu-yeon.

01:01:34.482 --> 01:01:38.027
The government will prioritize
the safety of the hostages

01:01:38.111 --> 01:01:43.074
and make every diplomatic effort
to rescue every one of them.

01:01:43.991 --> 01:01:45.618
Reporter Lee is on-site now.

01:01:54.794 --> 01:01:59.132
The number you have dialed is unavailable.
You'll be directed to voicemail after…

01:01:59.215 --> 01:02:00.591
HUSBAND

01:02:23.406 --> 01:02:24.240
Hello?

01:02:24.323 --> 01:02:25.992
What took you so long to pick up?

01:02:26.075 --> 01:02:27.493
Where are you? Are you okay?

01:02:28.286 --> 01:02:29.662
The negotiations are over.

01:02:30.246 --> 01:02:31.164
I'm coming home.

01:02:39.046 --> 01:02:41.090
We're ready for departure.

01:02:44.260 --> 01:02:45.470
I've been waiting.

01:02:45.553 --> 01:02:47.555
Why were you so hard to reach?

01:02:47.638 --> 01:02:49.766
I was in an area with no reception.

01:02:49.849 --> 01:02:50.683
But…

01:02:51.934 --> 01:02:53.269
what's with your tone?

01:02:53.352 --> 01:02:55.646
What's wrong with it, 406?

01:02:56.939 --> 01:02:58.733
Isn't it thrilling?

01:03:00.443 --> 01:03:01.277
"Thrilling"?

01:03:02.028 --> 01:03:05.531
Why? Do you miss her?

01:03:10.536 --> 01:03:11.537
Yes.

01:03:11.621 --> 01:03:12.997
I miss her.

01:03:13.080 --> 01:03:14.499
What do you miss?

01:03:14.582 --> 01:03:17.335
The chilly tone in her voice
when she threatened me.

01:03:18.461 --> 01:03:19.670
That sharp voice.

01:03:21.214 --> 01:03:22.381
Why did you like it?

01:03:24.509 --> 01:03:25.760
She didn't hold back.

01:03:26.677 --> 01:03:28.346
If you're upset with me

01:03:28.930 --> 01:03:30.973
and don't say anything, I won't know.

01:03:31.057 --> 01:03:34.894
And if you stay silent,
I might think I'm doing everything right.

01:03:36.103 --> 01:03:37.855
I like it when my wife

01:03:39.065 --> 01:03:40.399
doesn't hold back.

01:03:41.567 --> 01:03:43.069
Don't hold back anymore.

01:03:43.694 --> 01:03:45.029
Throw a tantrum, complain,

01:03:45.863 --> 01:03:46.989
and nag if you want.

01:03:47.698 --> 01:03:48.699
Do you promise?

01:03:50.159 --> 01:03:50.993
Yes.

01:03:51.077 --> 01:03:52.119
Do you swear?

01:03:52.870 --> 01:03:53.704
Yes.

01:03:54.288 --> 01:03:55.122
But,

01:03:56.249 --> 01:03:57.667
if I call,

01:03:57.750 --> 01:03:59.085
what will you do for me?

01:04:00.211 --> 01:04:03.256
Everything you ask me to, 406.

01:04:04.257 --> 01:04:07.760
So from now on,
call me for the rest of your life.

01:04:07.844 --> 01:04:10.346
I'll answer every time
as if it's the first call.

01:04:14.141 --> 01:04:16.727
Then starting now,
I'll tell you what I want.

01:04:16.811 --> 01:04:17.812
Listen carefully.

01:04:17.895 --> 01:04:19.188
What's that?

01:04:19.272 --> 01:04:23.276
Come back to me as soon as you can.

01:04:24.193 --> 01:04:26.529
Right now, into my arms.

01:04:27.530 --> 01:04:28.531
I'm on my way.

01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:37.123
There's a couple here now.

01:04:38.833 --> 01:04:44.046
The two have lived without being able
to open up to each other.

01:04:45.131 --> 01:04:46.799
Would things have been different…

01:04:47.884 --> 01:04:50.052
if they had been more honest

01:04:51.053 --> 01:04:52.305
and shown their true feelings?

01:04:53.723 --> 01:04:55.766
If they try to make an effort now,

01:04:57.435 --> 01:05:00.521
could they live
like any other ordinary couple?

01:05:02.356 --> 01:05:05.359
There's a couple here now.

01:05:06.569 --> 01:05:10.573
They don't hide their true feelings
and are honest with each other.

01:05:11.657 --> 01:05:16.954
They have promised to make
an effort to be happy together.

01:05:34.305 --> 01:05:37.224
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:07:08.899 --> 01:07:10.526
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
